      <div type="clause" n="El. 29">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 29</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 29" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="38" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa fæmnan beswice unbeweddode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ hire midslæpe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.2"/>, forgielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.3"/> hie ⁊ hæbbe hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.4"/> siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.5"/> him to wife. Gif ðære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.6"/> fæmnan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.7"/> fæder hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.8"/> ðonne sellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.9"/> nelle, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.10"/> he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.11"/> ðæt feoh æfter þam weotuman.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.12"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 29" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="38" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa fæmnan beswyce unbeweddude ⁊ hyre midslepe, forgylde hie ⁊ habbe hí siððan him to wife. Gyf ðære fæmnan fæder hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1-3"/> ðonne syllan nelle, ágife he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feoh æfter ðæm weotuman.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.2-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 29" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa fæmnan beswyce unbeweddode ⁊ hire midslæpe, forgylde heo ⁊ hæbbe hy syððan him to wife. Gif þære fæmnan fæder heo þonne syllan nelle, agife he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feoh æfter þam weotuman.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 29" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Si duxerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1-2"/> quis uirginem necdum desponsatam dormieritque cum ea, dotabit eam et habebit eam uxorem. Si pater uirginis dare noluerit, reddet pecuniam iuxta modum dotis, quam uirgines accipere consueuerunt.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 29" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="252" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hwa fæmnan beswice unbeweddode ⁊ hire midslæpe, forgielde hie ⁊ hæbbe hi siððan him to wife. Gif ðære fæmnan fæder hie ðonne sellan nelle, agife he ðæt feoh æfter þam weotuman.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="39" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand ein unverlobtes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.1"/> Mädchen verführt und bei ihr schläft, bezahle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.2"/> er sie und habe sie dann zum Weibe für sich. Wenn des Mädchens Vater sie jedoch [ihm] nicht geben will, so zahle jener [Verführer ihm Buss-]geld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.3"/> je nach dem Wittum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone seduces an unbetrothed girl and sleeps with her, let him pay for her and then have her as a wife for himself. But if the girl’s father will not give her [to him], then let that [seducer pay him compensation-]money according to the dower.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="253" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone deceives a virgin not yet betrothed and sleeps with her, let him compensate her and have her as a wife. If, however, her father will not give her [to him], let him give [her money] equivalent to the bride-price.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 22,16–17</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="39">Exodus 22.16; Exodus 22.17</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[Exodus 22, 16] | [22, 17]</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="253"><label>same term (weotuma)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-12">Af El 12</ref> <quote>weotuma is earlier used (see above, MP §12) to render pretium pudicitiae.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="253"><label>cf. (woman receives compensation)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref> <quote>Cf. Alfred §13, the language of which suggests that the woman herself was the recipient of compensation in cases of molestation or assault.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="253"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_18-1">Af 18.1</ref> <quote>Cf. Alfred §21, where it is established that a betrothed woman who fornicates with someone other than her intended husband is obligated to compensate the guarantor</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-odne <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-odne So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-sliepe <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-sliepe So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gylde <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> -gyld hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gylde So; -gyld hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hie <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hie So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ðon <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> syþþon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ðon So; syþþon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðær <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðær Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fæmnon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fæmnon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þ. hie <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þ. hie So; hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syllan nylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syllan nylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agyfe <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agyfe So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-toman <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-toman So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">39</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seduxerit <hi rend="italic">aus Vulg. zu bessern</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be corrected to seduxerit from Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> hie</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to hie</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">witoman weot., <hi rend="italic">ersteres von mod. Hd. durchstrichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">witoman weot., the former struck through by a modern hand</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘unverheiratet’; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Af 18, 1. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 7. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘unmarried’; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Af 18, 1. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 7. a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘vergelte’ Schmid; nämlich mit Brautkauf, anders als Vulg.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘requite’ Schmid; namely with the bride-price, unlike the Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vulg. meint, wie <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> El 12, Jungfernschaftspreis für das Mädchen, Af wohl Muntbrüche; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Unzucht 8. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Vulg., as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> El 12, means a virginity price for the girl; Af probably means compensation for breach of mund; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Unzucht 8. a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-29.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Wittum 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Wittum 1</seg></note>
      </div>
